a3"></rect><rect x="11" y="15" width="1" height="1" fill="#2bb3a3"></rect><rect x="12" y="15" width="1" height="1" fill="#efc19c"></rect><rect x="13" y="15" width="1" height="1" fill="#2b2233"></rect></g></svg><div class="mcp-id__text"><p class="mcp-kicker">🔬 Research Lab</p><h1 id="panel-title" class="mcp-id__name" tabindex="-1">Dan Nguyen</h1><p class="mcp-id__role">Software &amp; AI Engineer</p></div></header><p class="mcp-hint">Where Dan's research lives. The poster wall has a poster per project, the whiteboard has what he wants to study next, and the bench lays out his methods. His papers are on the shelf. For the rest of his story (roles, school, honors), head to the <a href="/dev">Dev Center</a>.</p><section class="mcp-card" aria-labelledby="next-title"><h2 id="next-title" class="mcp-h">Research interests</h2><p class="mcp-dim">The whiteboard is still being written.</p><div class="mcp-fastlane"><button type="button" class="mcp-btn mcp-btn--primary" data-open="posters">📜 Posters</button><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="whiteboard">✏️ Whiteboard</button><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="bench">🧪 Methods</button></div></section><section aria-labelledby="work-title"><h2 id="work-title" class="mcp-h">Research</h2><ul class="clean lab-list"><li class="mcp-card lab-item"><h3 class="lab-item__title">Saint Petersburg AI Agent</h3><p class="mcp-dim">Aug 2025 – Dec 2025</p><p>Can learned evaluators let Monte-Carlo Tree Search play a game with a large branching factor, and what do simulated games reveal about its balance?</p><p><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="posters" data-poster="p-st-petersburg">Read the poster 📜</button></p></li><li class="mcp-card lab-item"><h3 class="lab-item__title">3-Row Chomp: Making Byrnes Effective</h3><p class="mcp-dim">Aug 2025 – Present</p><p>Byrnes (2003) proved that in 3-row Chomp the losing positions of each row r eventually repeat with a fixed period, but his proof gives no bound on when the repetition starts. Can that preperiod N(r) be bounded explicitly?</p><p><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="posters" data-poster="p-chomp">Read the poster 📜</button></p></li><li class="mcp-card lab-item"><h3 class="lab-item__title">AI Engineer Intern</h3><p class="mcp-dim">KPMG · Berlin, DE · Jun 2025 – Aug 2025</p><p>How can LLM-generated question-answer data for an audit-expert model be validated before it is used for fine-tuning?</p><p><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="posters" data-poster="r-kpmg-ai-intern">Read the poster 📜</button></p></li><li class="mcp-card lab-item"><h3 class="lab-item__title">Data Scientist Intern</h3><p class="mcp-dim">KPMG · Berlin, DE · May 2024 – Aug 2024</p><p>Which clustering approach best separates audit risk, and does it hold up under expert review?</p><p><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="posters" data-poster="r-kpmg-ds-intern">Read the poster 📜</button></p></li><li class="mcp-card lab-item"><h3 class="lab-item__title">Healthcare Access Disparities Analysis</h3><p class="mcp-dim">Jan 2024 – May 2024</p><p>How unequal is healthcare access across Pennsylvania counties, and which gaps track worse outcomes?</p><p><button type="button" class="mcp-btn" data-open="posters" data-poster="p-healthcare">Read the poster 📜</button></p></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="methods-title"><h2 id="methods-title" class="mcp-h">Methods</h2><ul class="stack-chips"><li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #2a9bb5"><svg class="stack-chip__logo" viewBox="-1 -1 14 14" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="-1" y="-1" width="14" height="14" fill="#f4efe2"></rect><rect x="1" y="0" width="10" height="1" fill="#2a9bb5"></rect><rect x="0" y="1" width="12" height="1" fill="#2a9bb5"></rect><rect x="0" y="2" width="12" height="1" fill="#2a9bb5"></rect><rect x="0" y="3" width="3" height="1" fill="#2a9bb5"></rect><rect x="3" y="3" width="1" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="4" y="3" width="2